Package: better-screenshot
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: k-nowicki <now.nowicki@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: 1133
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libcairo2 (>= 1.10.0), libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0 (>= 2.23.0), libglib2.0-0t64 (>= 2.79.0), libgtk-3-0t64 (>= 3.21.4), libhandy-1-0 (>= 1.5.0), libx11-6, libxext6, dconf-gsettings-backend | gsettings-backend
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal-gnome
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/k-nowicki/better-screenshot
Description: screenshot tool that can capture a single monitor
 Better Screenshot is a fork of GNOME Screenshot for multi-monitor desktops.
 It adds a monitor drop-down to the capture dialog, so a screenshot can cover
 one physical screen instead of every monitor stitched together, and it
 remembers the choice between runs.
 .
 Captures are written straight to the pictures directory without a
 confirmation dialog, and the countdown holds no keyboard or pointer grab, so
 menus opened while it runs stay open and appear in the picture. A --monitor
 option takes a monitor number or a connector name such as DP-5, which makes
 it usable from a key binding.
 .
 It installs alongside gnome-screenshot rather than replacing it. Under X11 it
 reads the X server directly; under Wayland it uses the desktop portal, which
 cannot capture single windows or include the pointer.
